[size=5][b]Historical Doctrine (DLL edition)[/b][/size]

Adds a fifth doctrine, [b]Doctrine: Historical[/b], to all 20 skirmish missions (single player and coop): only the units that were really there for that battle, at that date, with those formations. They unlock in mixed packages (infantry, support, vehicles, tanks) for every sector you hold, and from 4 sectors you can deploy them anywhere on the map. The four vanilla doctrines are unchanged.

Unit lists of every mission, with icons: [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3840541746]unit guide on Steam[/url].

[b]Why a DLL edition?[/b]
The [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3838675132]Steam Workshop version[/url] ships modified copies of the 20 missions, so it can't be combined with other mods that change the same missions (for example [b]Spawn Menu[/b]): only one of them wins. This edition adds the Historical doctrine in memory to whatever version of the mission the game reads, so it works together with them, in any mod-list order.

Use [b]one or the other[/b], not both.

[b]Install[/b]
[list=1]
[*]Extract the zip into the game folder (the one that contains [i]binaries[/i] and [i]mods[/i]). If Windows asks, overwrite [i]version.dll[/i]: it's the shared loader of all my DLL mods.
[*]In the game: Options > Mods > enable [b]Historical Doctrine (DLL)[/b]. Disable or unsubscribe the Workshop version.
[*]In a skirmish, choose [b]Doctrine: Historical (...)[/b] in the mission options.
[/list]
[b]Every player in a coop match needs it[/b] (DLL + data mod), like any mod that changes the missions.

[b]Uninstall[/b]: delete [i]binaries\x64\goh_mods\historical_doctrine.dll[/i], the folder [i]binaries\x64\goh_mods\historical_doctrine[/i] and [i]mods\historical_doctrine[/i].

[b]If the doctrine doesn't show up in a mission[/b]: another mod changed that part of the mission too much, and the DLL left the mission as it is rather than half patching it. The log [i]%TEMP%\goh_historical_doctrine_call_to_arms.exe.log[/i] says which mission and why; please send it with your mod list.

Source code and technical details: [url=https://github.com/nicko996/goh-coop-mods/tree/main/mods/historical-doctrine]GitHub[/url]. Works with game version 1.067.

[b]My other mods[/b]: [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/calltoarmsgatesofhellostfront/mods/25]Coop Checkpoint[/url] (works together with this one from version 1.0.3: update it if you have an older one), [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/calltoarmsgatesofhellostfront/mods/24]Coop Game Speed[/url], [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/calltoarmsgatesofhellostfront/mods/22]Loot Highlight[/url], [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/calltoarmsgatesofhellostfront/mods/23]Inspect Preview[/url].
